    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this is a route-deviation dispute over trip TRP-00112 (Tampines to Raffles Place). The deviation is established on the trace, but the fare arithmetic leaves nothing to refund, so the charge you paid, Ms Rider, stands.\n\n1. Distance (POL-RD-01). The governing measure is the GPS trace, not the meter's rounded copy. EV-GPS-00112 records 22.40 km against the booked optimal of 17.60 km on EV-TRIP-00112: excess 4.80 km, or 27.27% of optimal. Both limbs are cleared (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. I have not used the trip record's 20.00 km / 13.6%, because POL-RD-01 forbids citing that field for the threshold test; the driver's argument that the excess be measured only from started_at (13.8%) is rejected for the same reason.\n\n2. Fare (POL-RD-02). The fare model is METERED. Recomputed fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 17.60 + 0.28 x 28.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls = 25.64. Charged total = 25.26. Refund = 25.26 - 25.64 = -0.38, floored at zero = 0.00. The optimal route is 4.8 km shorter but 7.8 minutes slower (28.0 optimal vs 20.2 actual), and the higher optimal time charge (7.84 vs the 5.66 billed) more than offsets the extra distance charge; you were not overcharged. A refund below SGD 0.50 is NO_ACTION as de minimis, and under POL-GEN-03 the charge stands as it is.\n\n3. The Paya Lebar Quarter stop. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00112, weight 1.0) shows the request and the driver's 'ok can', but the trace never comes within 200 m of the resolved waypoint - the nearest fix is 512 m away (fix 158, 18:45:00). Under POL-RD-04 the corroboration test fails and POL-RD-14 directs that no distance is excluded; the instruction did not cause the measured excess. The missed stop is a service matter on which this policy pays nothing - no fare line charges a stop or a missed stop. The driver is also wrong to say he made the stop: his own device trace does not support it.\n\n4. Impairment. EV-GPS-00112 and EV-TRIP-00112 are each impaired at weight 0.4 on issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT (they disagree about when the trip began by 13.5 minutes). That is schema-level impairment only: under POL-RD-07 the trace is policy-clean - no gap over 90 s (longest 0 s), no straight-line jump over 500 m, a 10 s sampling interval - so it still measures the excess, and the impairment enters POL-GEN-02 as a confidence discount, not as an escalation.\n\n5. No escalation. POL-RD-10(1): the fact that decides this ruling - that the fare recomputation yields no refund - is carried by EV-FARE-00112 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0, line items reconciling to the cent); the 0.4 impairment goes to the measured actual distance, and the outcome is NO_ACTION whether or not a deviation is established. POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged, the trace being policy-clean. POL-RD-10(4) is not engaged: the pickup and dropoff events on the two records align (18:17:50 / 18:18:40 and 18:52:20 / 18:52:12); the divergence is the meter start, not a pickup or dropoff timestamp. POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged: the driver's 'the app was acting up' excuse cites no advisory, and POL-RD-13 makes an uncited traffic assertion weightless rather than an escalation. POL-RD-10(7) is confined by POL-RD-14: a request that was made and a route that did not follow it are consistent, not contradictory evidence. The rider's arguments for escalation on the 0.4 cap and on the started_at conflict are therefore rejected.\n\n6. Other claims. No repeat-deviation pattern arises (1 flag over 296 trips in 90 days; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is not the field POL-RD-06 names), so there is no POL-RD-06 uplift and no conduct referral. There are no ERP gantries, tolls, airport surcharge or promo lines, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct. The driver's compensation claim (2.4 unbilled km x 0.75 = 1.80) is declined: it rests entirely on the 0.4-weighted trace and on exactly the disputed pre-start segment, so it cannot be granted above the confidence floor.\n\nThe monetary effect is nil, below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00. Either party may appeal this provisional ruling under POL-GEN-04."
  },
