    {
      "claim": "The driver blames the evening — 'the app was acting up' — but no external-traffic explanation is on file for this trip. EV-ADVIS-00112-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0: no LTA advisory covers the PIE or the ECP in the 18:14–18:52 window on 4 August 2026, which are the corridors the booked optimal route uses. Under POL-RD-13 an asserted traffic cause is tested against the trip's traffic_advisory and nothing else, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable on this record and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Nothing here reduces the measured excess.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00112-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The uncorroborated detour request is not an escalation trigger. POL-RD-10(7) is confined by POL-RD-14 to the case where the trace corroborates the rider's instruction in part, so that the excess attributable to it cannot be separated from the rest. Here the trace corroborates nothing about the waypoint, and a request that was made and a route that did not follow it are consistent with each other - that is a failed corroboration under POL-RD-04, not two contradictory bodies of comparable evidence. POL-RD-14 directs that the deviation be decided under POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 on the trace as measured, which also disposes of POL-GEN-07: a clause of the policy in force does license an outcome on these facts, so no residual-principles escalation is open.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00112 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    }
  ]
}

