  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Trip TRP-00112 (Tampines to One Raffles Place, 4 Aug 2026; charged S$25.26). The charge stands and no refund is due to the rider; no compensation is due to the driver.\n\n1) The fare. This was a METERED trip, so POL-RD-02 recomputes what the booked optimal route should have cost: base 3.80 + distance (0.75 x 17.6 km = 13.20) + time (0.28 x 28.0 min = 7.84) = 24.84, times the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare_breakdown (and nowhere else), plus the 0.80 platform fee. No ERP, toll, airport surcharge, waiting fee or promo applies, so the recomputed fare is 25.64. The rider paid 25.26. The optimal-route fare is therefore HIGHER than what was charged, so the refund is negative, floors at zero, and is below the 0.50 de minimis: NO_ACTION, and the 25.26 stands (POL-RD-02, POL-GEN-03). The reason is the optimal route's 28.0-minute duration - the rider was billed for only 20.2 minutes, and that saving more than offsets the extra distance.\n\n2) The distance conflict. The GPS trace begins at 18:18:40 and covers 2.38 km before the trip record's meter start of 18:32:10 - a 13 min 30 s disagreement. Both EV-GPS-00112 and EV-TRIP-00112 are IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 on issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, and that discount is carried through below. Measured over the whole trace the excess is 4.80 km / 27.27% (above the POL-RD-01 gate); measured over the recorded trip window it is 2.42 km / 13.8% (below it). I accept that nothing in the bundle conclusively decides which reading is right. It does not change the outcome: on the higher reading the deviation is established and POL-RD-02 still returns nothing (point 1); on the lower reading no deviation is established and POL-RD-01 gives the same NO_ACTION. The trace is NOT impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (no gaps, longest gap 0 s, 10 s sampling against the 30 s limb, no >500 m jumps), so the POL-RD-07 consequences and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation do not engage - the 0.4 is a POL-GEN-02 confidence down-weight only.\n\n3) The Paya Lebar Quarter stop. I accept the rider asked for the stop (MSG-00112-001, carrying a resolved waypoint_hint at Paya Lebar Quarter) and the driver agreed ('ok can', MSG-00112-002). But an extra-stop instruction excludes distance only if the trace corroborates it, and the trace never comes within 200 m of the waypoint - the nearest fix is 512.35 m (fix 158, 18:45:00). Under POL-RD-14 the request therefore excluded no distance; the driver's statement that he made the stop is unsupported by his own trace and carries no weight (POL-RD-08). No fare line charges a stop or missed-stop fee, so the missed stop is a service matter on which this policy pays nothing.\n\n4) The driver's 'app was acting up' explanation. Any external-traffic excuse is tested against this trip's traffic_advisory and nothing else. EV-ADVIS-00112-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 - no LTA advisory covers the PIE/ECP window. Under POL-RD-13 the excuse is tested against nothing and carries no weight (POL-RD-08); POL-RD-03 is unavailable and reduces no excess.\n\n5) Driver compensation. The driver's request for compensation for 'unbilled' distance is refused. It rests on the 2.4 km difference between the trace's 22.40 km and the billed 20.00 km, and that difference is exactly the contested pre-start head: the billed 20.00 km matches the trace after 18:32:10 (about 20.02 km). The same unresolved conflict that makes the deviation reading uncertain means the record does not establish that this distance was driven on this trip rather than carried over from a previous job, so no shortfall is established and nothing is paid.\n\n6) Escalation and referrals. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The artifacts' pickup and dropoff events agree (arrival 18:17:50 vs first fix 18:18:40, 50 s; end 18:52:20 vs last fix 18:52:12, 8 s), so POL-RD-10(4) is not engaged - the divergence is the internal meter start, handled under POL-GEN-02 and immaterial either way. POL-RD-10(7) is confined by POL-RD-14 to the partly-corroborated case. POL-RD-10(1) is not engaged because the fact that decides the money sits on the clean EV-FARE-00112 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0), not on the impaired instruments. No billing-integrity defect exists under POL-RD-09(4). On POL-RD-06 the driver's trailing-90-day record (1 deviation flag over 296 completed trips) is below both limbs, so there is no pattern, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral; no other profile field has been used (POL-GEN-01).\n\nConfidence 0.9: the deciding money facts (charged 25.26 and the recomputed 25.64) are carried by the clean fare_breakdown, so the ruling is not driven below the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect is nil, below the 8.00 execution threshold. Two claims were discarded at the citation check: a rider claim citing the missing traffic advisory without naming its issue code, and a driver claim citing the impaired trace without naming its issue code.\n\nThis ruling was made without human review. Either party may appeal once under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver blames the evening — 'the app was acting up' — but no external-traffic explanation is on file for this trip. EV-ADVIS-00112-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0: no LTA advisory covers the PIE or the ECP in the 18:14–18:52 window on 4 August 2026, which are the corridors the booked optimal route uses. Under POL-RD-13 an asserted traffic cause is tested against the trip's traffic_advisory and nothing else, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable on this record and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Nothing here reduces the measured excess.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00112-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The uncorroborated detour request is not an escalation trigger. POL-RD-10(7) is confined by POL-RD-14 to the case where the trace corroborates the rider's instruction in part, so that the excess attributable to it cannot be separated from the rest. Here the trace corroborates nothing about the waypoint, and a request that was made and a route that did not follow it are consistent with each other - that is a failed corroboration under POL-RD-04, not two contradictory bodies of comparable evidence. POL-RD-14 directs that the deviation be decided under POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 on the trace as measured, which also disposes of POL-GEN-07: a clause of the policy in force does license an outcome on these facts, so no residual-principles escalation is open.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00112 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
