    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To both parties. [Rider] — what you paid ($25.26) is less than what the booked optimal route would cost under the fare model, so there is nothing to refund, and the fare stands.\n\nThe arithmetic (POL-RD-02): the booked optimal route (PIE westbound then ECP) is 17.6 km and 28.0 min. Recomputation = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 17.6 = 13.20 distance + 0.28 x 28.0 = 7.84 time) x surge 1.0 (read from the fare breakdown's surge_multiplier, and nowhere else) + 0.80 platform fee = $25.64. No ERP, tolls, surcharge, waiting fee or promo apply. $25.64 exceeds the $25.26 charged, so the refund floors at zero, and it is below the $0.50 de-minimis floor: NO_ACTION. Your route was longer (20.0 km vs 17.6 km) but your time was shorter (20.2 min vs 28.0 min), and the time saving ($2.18) more than offsets the extra distance ($1.80) — you were undercharged by about $0.38, not overcharged.\n\nYour deviation claim: the trace records 22.40 km against the 17.60 km optimal, a 4.80 km / 27.27% excess, which would clear the POL-RD-01 gate (over 20% and over 0.8 km), and POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern the trip record's rounded 20.0 km. But the trace and the trip record disagree about when the trip began (18:18:40 vs 18:32:10 — 13 min 30 s), and measured from the recorded trip start the excess is only 2.42 km / 13.8%. The disagreement does not decide the money: on either figure the POL-RD-02 refund is nil.\n\nThe Paya Lebar Quarter stop (POL-RD-04 / POL-RD-14): you asked for it (MSG-00112-001) and [driver] agreed ('ok can', MSG-00112-002), but the trace never comes within 200 m of the waypoint — the nearest fix is 512 m at 18:45:00 — so the instruction did not cause the excess, no distance is excluded, and the policy pays nothing for a missed stop: no stop fee appears on the receipt, and the distance-and-time lines recompute to zero.\n\n[Driver] — your account that you made the stop ('waited about four minutes there') is not supported: the trace never comes within 512 m of the waypoint, so it carries no weight (POL-RD-08). Your compensation claim for distance billed below the trace is refused: the 2.4 km shortfall is exactly the disputed pre-start segment, and against the recorded trip window the billed 20.0 km matches the 20.02 km driven, so no shortfall over 1.0 km is established.\n\nEvidence and confidence: EV-GPS-00112 and EV-TRIP-00112 are both IMPAIRED on the pre-pass at weight 0.4, issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT — an alignment defect between the trace and the trip record. It is not a POL-RD-07 defect: the trace has no gap over 90 s (max 0 s), no jump over 500 m, and a 10 s sampling interval, so it is policy-clean and governs the POL-RD-01 threshold. The impairment is disclosed and priced into confidence, but the deciding arithmetic (the zero refund) is carried by the COMPLETE fare breakdown at weight 1.0, so it does not cap the ruling below the 0.70 floor. Confidence 0.80.\n\nNo POL-RD-06 conduct referral: 1 deviation flag over 296 trips is neither the 3-flag nor the 0.05-ratio test, and the deviation is not MATERIAL (4.80 km < 8.0 km; 27.3% < 50%). No POL-RD-09(4) billing finding: there is no ERP, toll or surcharge line, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. No POL-RD-10 escalation: the trip identifiers match, the pickup and dropoff events align across the artifacts (arrival 18:17:50 vs first fix 18:18:40; ended_at 18:52:20 vs last fix 18:52:12), the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), and the uncorroborated PLQ instruction is a failed corroboration (POL-RD-14), not the contradiction POL-RD-10(7) describes. The monetary effect is nil, below the $8.00 execution threshold. The contested amount was $6.00; none of it is refunded."
  },
